            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FLA02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Flaxman</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1755-07-06">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1826-12-07"/>
                    <occupation>sculptor</occupation>
                    <occupation>decorative designer</occupation>
                    <occupation>illustrator</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>John Flaxman exhibited at the Royal Academy from the 1770s and later spent 
  seven years in Rome in 1787-94, which helped to develop and secure his international reputation. The entries in the diary cluster betwen 1797 and 1810.  The
  first contact is at the Milton Gallery on 17 May 1800, but this may simply be noting Flaxman's presence rather than indicating a contact.  Flaxman's appearance in the 
  1796 list suggests that they first meet in 1802, although this is deduced from the fact that 1803 is given as the date after the list of names in which Flaxman appears.
  Marshall suggests that while Godwin is keen to make his acquaintance, Flaxman avoids him. </p>
                        <p>Godwin recorded his death in 1826.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 8, fol. 6: 19 November 1802</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 8, fol. 73: 16 July 1804</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Marshall, p. 259.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
